c from main base 250bceb80be4cfc9f7c844d888af864fc1d38d25. Ordinary Django settings and a parent-owned disposable server preserve standard test-runner isolation and original failures. Python browser/Go HTTP Live examples reuse one app across sequential cases; Go/Python guides explain independent serial/parallel Forks.\n\nLive CI delegates only duplicate Ubuntu check/macOS integration invocations already owned by Development on the same full PR/main event. Other scopes and standalone events retain local canonical work. Compiler/module caching preserves exact-source builds, invalidates restored test results and keeps both-host Live race tests fresh. No product API/runtime/guest/generated/dependency-pin/version/release changes or exploratory-history merge are included.\n\nReviewed head d389306 and actual PR CI source 3ed2c8e0790499c215869e33154272b062c35a88 have identical trees. All 20 jobs passed: [Django40492425975](https://github.com/masahitojp/mariamem/actions/runs/40492425975), [Live40492426087](https://github.com/masahitojp/mariamem/actions/runs/40492426087), [Development40492425939](https://github.com/masahitojp/mariamem/actions/runs/40492425939) and [dump regression40492426188](https://github.com/masahitojp/mariamem/actions/runs/40492426188). Django's native2 + guest4 cells include original error/partial-DDL/no-admission/cleanup oracles. Live includes both-host/Python public examples, mutations and installed consumers. Original receipts retain that source identity. Subsequent changes are documentation/evidence only and require their own fresh strict-base checks.\n\nAccepted limits: exact new manual parallel guide snippets were statically checked, not executed; existing parallel runtime anchors remain. Django is a bounded recipe, not blanket compatibility or a new adapter, and its workflow is not a required protection context. First compiler-cache fills succeeded, but warm-cache speedup is unmeasured. Guide-only skip policy and broader interruption coverage remain separate decisions.\n\nThe Human approved main adoption. The decision, receipt summary and continuation procedure are in docs/reviews/v06x-dogfood-main-adoption.md. Keep check/integration/Live required gate app-bound, strict and admin-enforced; no bypass or policy change is authorized. On the Human's report of this updated head's CI completion, reread exact head/base, all candidate checks including Django and protection, then continue the already-approved adoption through this PR without another approval request. Record actual main/squash identity and protection before declaring completion. Qualification, version and publication remain separate.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:56Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T12:14:05Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"730bd17c935928dd37e2cd7df14aa115c40e89a7","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"masahitojp:candidate/v06-dogfood-recipes","ref":"candidate/v06-dogfood-recipes","repo":{"id":1383417913,"node_id":"R_kgDOUnVIOQ","name":"mariamem","full_name":"masahitojp/mariamem","owner":{"login":"masahitojp","id":42042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp","html_url":"https://github.com/masahitojp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/masahitojp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"htt